## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have these installed:

- **Python 3.10+** → [Download](https://python.org/downloads)
- **Node.js 18+** → [Download](https://nodejs.org)
- **Git** → [Download](https://git-scm.com)
- **Google Gemini API Key** → [Get free key](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)

> 💡 No GPU required. Runs on any CPU-based laptop.

---

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/knowledge-evolution-platform.git
cd knowledge-evolution-platform
```

---

### 2️⃣ Backend Setup

```bash
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate it
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**Configure environment variables:**

Create a `.env` file inside `backend/`:

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./knowledge.db
UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```

**Run the backend server:**

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Backend will run at → **http://localhost:8000**
API docs (Swagger) at → **http://localhost:8000/docs**

---

### 3️⃣ Frontend Setup

Open a **new terminal**:

```bash
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run dev server
npm run dev
```

Frontend will run at → **http://localhost:5173**

---

### 4️⃣ Access the Application

Open your browser and go to:

👉 **http://localhost:5173**

You should see the **Dashboard** page.

---

## 🔑 Environment Variables

### Backend (`backend/.env`)

| Variable | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Your Google Gemini API key | `AIza...` |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Database connection string | `sqlite:///./knowledge.db` |
| `UPLOAD_DIR` | Where uploads are stored | `./uploads` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Logging level | `INFO` |

### Frontend (`frontend/.env`)

| Variable | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `VITE_API_URL` | Backend API base URL | `http://localhost:8000` |

⚠️ **NEVER commit `.env` files to GitHub.** They are in `.gitignore`.

---

## 📡 API Endpoints

### 📄 Documents

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/api/documents/upload` | Upload a document |
| `GET` | `/api/documents` | List all documents |
| `GET` | `/api/documents/{id}` | Get document details |
| `DELETE` | `/api/documents/{id}` | Delete a document |

### 🧠 Knowledge

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/knowledge` | List all knowledge items |
| `GET` | `/api/knowledge/{id}` | Get knowledge item |
| `POST` | `/api/knowledge/search` | Semantic search |

### 🤖 Agents

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/api/agents/knowledge-miner/run` | Trigger Knowledge Miner |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/validator/run` | Trigger Validator |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/summarizer/run` | Trigger Summarizer |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/graph-builder/run` | Trigger Graph Builder |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/memory-manager/run` | Trigger Memory Manager |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/orchestrate` | Run full pipeline |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/logs` | Get agent activity logs |

### 🕸️ Graph

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/graph/nodes` | Get all graph nodes |
| `GET` | `/api/graph/edges` | Get all graph edges |
| `GET` | `/api/graph/visualize` | Full graph for UI |
| `POST` | `/api/graph/rebuild` | Rebuild entire graph |

### 📊 Dashboard

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/dashboard/stats` | Overall statistics |
| `GET` | `/api/dashboard/activity` | Recent agent activity |

---

## 🗄️ Database Schema

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `documents` | Uploaded files metadata |
| `knowledge_items` | Extracted structured facts |
| `validations` | Fact-check results |
| `summaries` | Generated document summaries |
| `graph_nodes` | Concepts in knowledge graph |
| `graph_edges` | Relationships between concepts |
| `agent_logs` | Agent activity tracking |

Full schema → see [`database/schema.sql`](database/schema.sql)

